   "notes": "Canvas shelter (sheet 066, remade): four 1.3 square timber posts on tapered stone footings (2.1 base, 1.30 high; post tops 12.0 for the right pair, 10.4 for the left; centres 14.0 x 10.4), a 0.8 ridge beam lashed level along the tall posts' inner faces, one cream canvas (closed 0.10 slab) tied into gold X-lashings at the four corners, the back-right corner up under the beam, lowest underside >= 6.9 (walk under); a red three-tailed banner with a white diamond and arrow bar, hung by red bands from a rod lashed to the front-left post; a square lantern with Neon glass on an iron bracket under the front-right corner (heat_glow); a plank table (top 2.60) with a paper and two bottles, two benches (seats 1.50), a closed X-braced crate and a lidded barrel. Seat and lantern points stored."
